    "narrative": "As we head into today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 74.12 efficiency score. While he faces Mize, the projection benefits from a favorable dynamic platoon advantage and a solid spot in the order, making him our primary engine for both counting stats and the stolen bases that are so vital to our strategy. Similarly, **Brice Turang** (69.08) and **Isaac Paredes** (67.84) represent our strongest daily plays. **Brice Turang**\u2019s score is buoyed significantly by a high-upside matchup against McGreevy, while **Isaac Paredes** is maximized by a park factor that clearly favors his profile, despite a slight drag from platoon splits. Keep an eye on **James Wood** (64.46) as well; his elite xwOBA and lead-off spot against a lefty give him a high floor, showcasing why he continues to be a staple in our lineup.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s bench was **Josh Naylor**. He sat on the bubble with a score of 44.56, but was ultimately excluded due to a brutal matchup against the left-handed Detmers, which compounded with a park penalty to push him below our preferred threshold. While **Josh Naylor** provides dependable power, our current configuration of **Austin Riley** and **Mickey Moniak**\u2014the latter of whom is thriving with a +14% platoon boost\u2014offers a superior efficiency profile against their respective right-handed opponents. \n\nRisks today are concentrated on the wind and opposing arms. **Trevor Story** and **Seiya Suzuki** both see their scores clipped by nearly 10 points due to adverse wind conditions, though **Seiya Suzuki** remains a startable asset. We are also wary of **Vinnie Pasquantino** drawing Williams, whose sub-3.00 xERA is the most intimidating hurdle on today's board. Managers should monitor these wind-effected games closely; if the conditions shift, it may alter the viability of **Trevor Story** late in the day. **Jose Caballero** remains a high-variance play, but we are deploying him specifically for his 87% stolen base threat against the slow delivery of Rogers, which is a calculated gamble to keep us competitive in the scarcest category.",
